---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import CommandBlock from '../../components/content/CommandBlock.astro';
import ScreenshotPlaceholder from '../../components/ui/ScreenshotPlaceholder.astro';
---

<GuideLayout 
  title="Installation Guide"
  guideType="installation"
>
  <h1>Installation Guide</h1>
  
  <h2>Requirements</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Component</th>
        <th>Version</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Minecraft</td>
        <td>1.20.6</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Fabric Loader</td>
        <td>0.19.3</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Java</td>
        <td>21</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Client Installation</h2>
  
  <h3>Option 1: Using Fabric Installer (Recommended)</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Download Fabric installer from <a href="https://fabricmc.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://fabricmc.net/</a></li>
    <li>Run installer: Select "Client" installation</li>
    <li>Select Minecraft 1.20.6 and Loader 0.19.3</li>
    <li>Create new profile in Minecraft Launcher</li>
    <li>Install MCDG mod:
      <ul>
        <li>Navigate to <code>.minecraft/mods/</code></li>
        <li>Copy <code>mcdg-0.1.0.jar</code> to mods folder</li>
        <li>Launch Minecraft with Fabric profile</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Option 2: Using MultiMC/Prism Launcher</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Create new instance</li>
    <li>Select Minecraft 1.20.6</li>
    <li>Add Fabric Loader component</li>
    <li>Add MCDG mod as external mod</li>
    <li>Launch instance</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Option 3: ATLauncher</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Create new instance</li>
    <li>Select Minecraft 1.20.6 with Fabric</li>
    <li>Add MCDG mod to mods folder</li>
    <li>Launch instance</li>
  </ol>

  <ScreenshotPlaceholder 
    title="Launcher Instance Setup"
    description="MultiMC/Prism launcher showing instance configuration"
    width="100%"
    height="300px"
  />

  <h2>Server Installation</h2>

  <h3>Step 1: Prepare Server Environment</h3>
  
  <h4>Install Java 21</h4>
  <CommandBlock 
    command="sudo apt update && sudo apt install openjdk-21-jre-headless"
    description="Ubuntu/Debian"
  />
  <CommandBlock 
    command="sudo yum install java-21-openjdk-headless"
    description="CentOS/RHEL"
  />
  <CommandBlock 
    command="java -version"
    description="Verify installation"
  />

  <h4>Create Server Directory</h4>
  <CommandBlock 
    command="mkdir -p /opt/mcdg-server && cd /opt/mcdg-server"
    description="Create and enter server directory"
  />

  <h4>Download Minecraft Server</h4>
  <CommandBlock 
    command="wget https://launcher.mojang.com/v1/objects/8f3112a1049751c472beb9697ae9425ac0d371a9/server.jar"
    description="Download Minecraft 1.20.6 server jar"
  />
  <CommandBlock 
    command="echo 'eula=true' > eula.txt"
    description="Accept EULA"
  />

  <h4>Install Fabric Loader</h4>
  <CommandBlock 
    command="wget https://maven.fabricmc.net/net/fabricmc/fabric-installer/1.0.1/fabric-installer-1.0.1.jar"
    description="Download Fabric installer"
  />
  <CommandBlock 
    command="java -jar fabric-installer-1.0.1.jar server -mcversion 1.20.6 -loader 0.19.3"
    description="Install server"
  />

  <h3>Step 2: Install MCDG Mod</h3>
  
  <h4>Install Mod Files</h4>
  <CommandBlock 
    command="mkdir -p /opt/mcdg-server/mods"
    description="Create mods directory"
  />
  <CommandBlock 
    command="cp mcdg-0.1.0.jar /opt/mcdg-server/mods/"
    description="Copy MCDG mod"
  />

  <h3>Step 3: Configure Server</h3>
  
  <h4>Basic Server Configuration</h4>
  <p>Edit <code>server.properties</code>:</p>
  <pre><code># Basic Settings
server-name=MCDG Disc Golf Server
motd=Welcome to MCDG Disc Golf Server!
max-players=20
difficulty=peaceful
gamemode=survival
hardcore=false

# World Settings
level-name=world
level-seed=
level-type=default
generate-structures=true

# Network Settings
server-port=25565
server-ip=
pvp=false
enable-query=false
enable-rcon=false

# Performance Settings
view-distance=10
simulation-distance=10
max-tick-time=60000
max-world-size=29999984

# Player Settings
white-list=false
enforce-whitelist=false
spawn-protection=0
spawn-monsters=false
spawn-animals=true
spawn-npcs=true</code></pre>

  <h2>Resource Pack</h2>
  <p>MCDG-Test-Resources is <strong>built into the mod jar</strong> and is <strong>auto-enabled by default</strong>.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>You do <strong>not</strong> need to manually enable it in Options → Resource Packs</li>
    <li>If you ever need to reinstall it manually, use the standalone <code>MCDG-Test-Resources.zip</code> in the resourcepacks folder</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Issue</th>
        <th>Fix</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Release ID mismatch</td>
        <td>Confirm <code>VERSION.txt</code> matches across all participants</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Fabric / Java version mismatch</td>
        <td>Verify Fabric Loader <code>0.19.3</code> and Java <code>21</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Resource pack visuals differ</td>
        <td>Ensure <code>MCDG-Test-Resources</code> is loaded. It is auto-enabled, but check <strong>Options → Resource Packs</strong> if needed</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Command permission fails</td>
        <td>Ensure OP level >= 2 on dedicated server</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>G keybind conflict</td>
        <td>Rebind in <strong>Options → Controls → MCDG</strong></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</GuideLayout>
